    "body": "pulse task #2829 \u00b7 generation 1.\n\n<!-- pulse-operation:c7a1e083d337b825d441338cabeae0fa -->\n\nassigned to @PORTALSURFER. the frozen task plan is retained in pulse and copied below.\n\n# Pulse task #2829: Outline every device with a thin rounded border\n\nOperation: c7a1e083d337b825d441338cabeae0fa\nAssignee: PORTALSURFER (Pulse #1, GitHub ID 41680373)\n\nUser requests a thin border around EACH device with rounded corners. Implement consistently in the existing shared native device shell/panel styling for Track and Return chains and all device kinds using that shell; avoid separate hand-drawn borders in individual EQ/Sampler/Operator widgets. Reuse application theme geometry/stroke tokens and current corner radius; introduce only a minimal shared styling adjustment if a token is missing. The outline should remain visible and subtle in ordinary and selected/hover/focused states, with consistent rounded clipping and no double stroke, square-corner bleed, cropped bottom edge or changed panel size/hit targets.\n\nPreserve #2472/merged PR207's header-only selection highlight: this is an ordinary boundary outline for every device, not permission to bring back a full-body selection accent. Preserve active/disabled state legibility and the current controls/focus/drag/reorder/remove behavior. Verify actual rendered shell at representative widths/heights, adjacent devices, selected/unselected and Track/Return paths; meaningful geometry/painter check proportional to the small styling change. Do not expand into EQ redesign2800, unrelated parameter layouts or DSP/schema changes. Coordinate with source1's active402device-panel focus repair and source5's406EQ field so only one writer changes shared shell files at a time.\n\nFocused canonical PR, targeted checks, immutable exact-source handoff to the sole merge agent; unmerged source stays In Progress, Ready for Review only after verified merge. Root owns any native visual acceptance, no live user-app actions, installation or forced quit.\n\ncreated by pulse shared PR intake/start task. builds, checks and merging follow the repository's own instructions.",
